SUMMARY:Author Talk: "The Cruelest Game" by Matthew Futterman
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 9 spots left\nSt
 atus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/201348
 \n\nCelebrate an unforgettable summer of tennis with an inside look at the
  game beyond center court. Join acclaimed sports journalist and bestsellin
 g author Matthew Futterman for his first Boston appearance on the book tou
 r for The Cruelest Game\, an illuminating exploration of the ambition\, re
 silience\, and sacrifice required to succeed at the highest levels of prof
 essional tennis. Through remarkable access and previously untold stories\,
  Futterman pulls back the curtain on the sport to examine the immense pres
 sures facing established champions and the next generation of players comp
 eting for their place among tennis’s elite.\n\nJoining Futterman in conv
 ersation are former world No. 7 tennis player and Olympic silver medalist\
 , Tim Mayotte\, and The New Yorker staff writer\, Louisa Thomas\, who pens
  the publication’s Sporting Scene column. Together\, they will bring per
 spectives from the court and the press box to a wide-ranging conversation 
 about professional tennis at a pivotal moment. As familiar legends make wa
 y for a new generation of stars\, the evening will explore the changing la
 ndscape of the sport\, the realities behind its most celebrated victories\
 , and the personal price of pursuing greatness on the world stage. \n\n*T
 his event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary li
 ght bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancella
 tions be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/201348
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
